# M5 red team: stale translations (user/root/src/redteam/vm.rs). The root
# task maps frames at 0x80_0000_0000 in its own VSpace and writes through
# each, so the translation is in the TLB, then takes the access away; a
# prober thread in the same VSpace (no CR3 write between them) touches the
# address and must fault. Covered: Frame_Unmap, Frame_Remap to read-only,
# CNode_Delete and CNode_Revoke of the frame, PageTable_Unmap,
# PageDirectory_Unmap, PDPT_Unmap, CNode_Delete of the page table, a revoke
# and reuse of the frame's untyped, and a 2 MiB frame unmapped and
# remapped read-only. Frame_Map at USER_TOP, 2^47, page 0 and in the
# kernel half is refused.
cmdline: test=redteam-tlb
exit: success
expect: microL4 kernel
expect: root: cmdline "test=redteam-tlb"
expect: redteam: tlb: after Frame_Unmap, a read of 0x8000001000 faults
expect: redteam: tlb: after Frame_Remap to read-only, a write of 0x8000001000 faults (fsr 0x7)
expect: redteam: tlb: after CNode_Delete of the mapped copy, a read
expect: redteam: tlb: after CNode_Revoke of the frame, a read
expect: redteam: tlb: after PageTable_Unmap, a read
expect: redteam: tlb: after PageDirectory_Unmap, a read
expect: redteam: tlb: after PDPT_Unmap, a read
expect: redteam: tlb: after CNode_Delete of the page table, a read
expect: redteam: tlb: after a revoke and reuse of its untyped, a read of 0x8000003000 faults
expect: redteam: tlb: after Frame_Unmap of a 2 MiB frame, a read
expect: redteam: tlb: after Frame_Remap of a 2 MiB frame to read-only, a write
expect: redteam: tlb: Frame_Map at USER_TOP, 2^47, page 0 and in the kernel half: refused
expect: TEST PASS
expect: DEBUG HALT 0 from TCB
